# Build-time configuration for the frontend. Copy to `.env.local` for local
# use, or set these in the Vercel project's Environment Variables.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables at build time, so changing either of these
# requires a rebuild (on Vercel: a redeploy, not just a settings save).
#
# Both are optional. Left unset they resolve to same-origin relative paths,
# which is what the two non-Vercel deployments need: the FastAPI server
# serving the built bundle out of muscriptor/web_dist, and `pnpm dev`, whose
# Vite proxy forwards the same paths to a backend (see vite.config.ts).

# Origin of the muscriptor server: /transcribe, /instruments, /auralize,
# /sheets, /soundfonts, /health. This is the GPU box (e.g. a Vast.ai instance).
# It must allow this site's origin in its CORS allowlist.
VITE_TRANSCRIBE_API_BASE=https://muscriptor.example.com

# Origin of the standalone chord service: /analyze, /health. A CPU-only
# Hugging Face Space running BTC chord recognition. Unset means "no separate
# service" — the app then uses the chords the muscriptor server already sends
# with the transcription. Also CORS-gated (ALLOWED_ORIGINS on the Space).
VITE_CHORD_API_BASE=https://owner-muscriptor-chords.hf.space
